well circa celebrating its grand opening  today it's the first adults-only casino  resort in las vegas and now the tallest  north of the strip of course we were  there when the casino opened back in  october but the hotel officially opened  today  our hector mejia got the great  assignment of checking out one of the  brand new hotel rooms  we are on the 25th floor this is a king  corner room we have the seating area  here and really panoramic views of the  entire valley  from the mountain ranges off to the  views of downtown  look at this and right below we have  stadium swim  sports here a huge theme at circa and  they have a lot of neat features one  thing you will not  find is a telephone and that is because  this tablet  replaces the traditional telephone you  can actually make a phone call with this  tablet  another neat feature is the lighting you  can actually select the type of mood you  want from  candlelight to uh let's say let's try  happy hour a little bit more dim or if  you want to brighten things up you just  click  the bright button this whole project has  a reported price tag  of one billion dollars the artwork  around circa pays tribute to las vegas  golden era  and just like the casino floor the  design in the rooms reflects different  eras  something new mixed with shapes forms  and colors that were popular in  different era such as  the 20s 50s the 80s and the very first  guests had the chance to check in early  on saturday in what was called  the world's earliest check-in with  people checking in two days early for  free  the property created around fifteen  hundred jobs at a time when other places  are cutting back because of the pandemic  with the hotel tower opening today it  finalizes the phased  opening of circa it was a great  thing for just with how everything is in  the world right now that we were able to  phase the openings so that  having the casino open it kind of gave  us a couple months to really  kind of work things out and and kind of  get our feet underneath us and now with  opening the hotel um obviously is a huge  thing for downtown las vegas and las  vegas in general  the hotel tower is the tallest north of  the las vegas strip with 60 floors  it'll have 777 rooms  the property already has the title for  having the world's  largest sports book and it's hard to  believe construction for this began in  february of 2019 and here's another neat  thing  a lot of the artwork you'll find in the  rooms was designed  by local artists reporting from the  brand new circa resort hector mejia  8 news now it's a beautiful building  hector thanks
 

